            <ArticleTitle>[Immunoglobulin content in the blood serum of myocardial infarct patients].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>37-42</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The content of serum immunoglobulins G, A, and M was studied in 143 patients suffering from myocardial infarction and in 119 donors. It was found that in patients with myocardial infarction the level of serum immunoglobulins depends on the size of the necrotic focus, the developing complications and the concomitant diseases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
